WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.409 --> 00:00:10.340
We have to make sure we have appropriate communications

2
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.350
about current and potential threats to keep awareness high.

3
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.290
We could even encourage friendly competition between

4
00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:18.569
departments to spot the most fishing attempts.

5
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.229
We can offer friendly reminders like a little

6
00:00:21.239 --> 00:00:24.040
squishy stress ball that says lock your computer.

7
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.879
There are also automatic systems that lock the computer automatically.

8
00:00:27.889 --> 00:00:28.909
When you step away.

9
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.970
It is important to make sure we get positive feedback about our training,

10
00:00:32.979 --> 00:00:35.270
ensuring it is appropriate and understood.

11
00:00:35.779 --> 00:00:39.889
Make sure the organization's leaders understand the importance of training and

12
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.580
working to promote and improve the

13
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.250
information security environment of the organization

14
00:00:44.799 --> 00:00:47.490
and provide the opportunity for personnel to practice

15
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.389
what they've learned with exercises and simulations.

16
00:00:50.959 --> 00:00:54.700
Occasionally send simulated fishing emails for example and

17
00:00:54.709 --> 00:00:56.970
give them positive feedback for reporting it.

18
00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:01.020
Depending on the organization's culture and risk profile

19
00:01:01.029 --> 00:01:04.650
awareness training should be a positive experience for everyone

20
00:01:04.779 --> 00:01:08.209
and not punitive unless it is absolutely necessary.